id: pm-beads-i59r
title: Reconcile Beads snapshots against an acknowledged base and live tracker
description: "Acceptance: concurrent local and external edits conflict deterministically; external omissions only propose deletion and never delete by default; stale-base application refuses. Deliver typed SDK and CLI, compact TOON/JSON reports, typed remedies, README/example, non-git public tracker validation and npm/Bun CI release gates."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-21T20:31:04.869Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-22T16:38:29.780Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[28]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-21T20:31:26.295Z",codex-agent,"Overlap recheck: pm-beads import --upsert strategies update/skip/fail and beads diff compare incoming/live data without an acknowledged external base. Core bulk keyed upsert likewise lacks external base ownership. Jira import uses SDK transactions and ADO owns remote revision assertions; their provider reconciliation stays in those adapters. This feature owns only Beads snapshot acknowledgement and three-way field classification, reusing core item versions and workspace transactions. Tracker-only PR #159 and its eight items are excluded."
  "2026-10-21T20:39:13.625Z",codex-agent,"Implemented source-scoped acknowledged bases, pure field-level three-way plans, bounded summaries and SDK/CLI preview/apply workflows. Real non-git tracker tests verify disjoint merges, conflicts, persistent omission proposals, stale-base and stale-tracker refusal. Application uses core history hashes and workspace journals; new identities are created before relationship wiring. Targeted failure testing caught and corrected SDK dependency flag syntax and empty-edge clearing requirements. Full release coverage remains assigned to CI because the host is saturated."
  "2026-10-21T20:46:49.139Z",codex-agent,"Expanded overlap check: pm-todos sync rewrites its current checkbox file after import/export, while CSV transaction imports and Linear/GitHub sync retain adapter-specific contracts; none supplies an acknowledged Beads external base. Added real SDK rollback, exact journal replay, writer-lock revalidation and git-free PATH regressions. Core explicit-unset audit suffixes are now recognized when inspecting transaction markers. CI now executes the unchanged full release:check script under npm and Bun on Node 22 and 26."
  "2026-10-21T20:49:22.744Z",codex-agent,"Public-data proof: archived public main tracker at 104ee0d795b6d9b5c305686209d8ab1c6b540bc7 into a fresh non-git tracker. 93 baseline items; 93 unchanged. A 93-record incoming snapshot plus synthetic concurrent edits yielded 1 deterministic field conflict. Conflict-free variant applied 2 changes, preserved 2 local-only edits and 1 deletion proposal; item count became 94. Conflict, stale-base and stale-tracker refusals passed. Original public tracker tree remained unchanged. Compact JSON was 773 bytes versus 135695 bytes for the full review plan; elapsed 6.36 seconds. Reproducible command: node test/public-reconcile-validation.ts."
  "2026-10-21T20:54:25.896Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof: reverting only the classifier to unconditional upsert made the truth-table regression fail (1 failure); suppressing omission proposals made the real non-git regression fail (0 versus 1 proposal); reverting the apply function to trust the preview without base validation/reclassification made the stale-base regression fail with Missing expected rejection. Restored the implementation after every experiment. New reconciliation source measured 100% lines, branches and functions in targeted coverage. Real compiled CLI also passed acknowledgement, JSON/TOON preview, apply and stale refusal with git absent from PATH. Raised only the declared compatible host floor to the already-pinned 2026.10.15 SDK; no development dependency was upgraded."
  "2026-10-21T20:57:29.456Z",codex-agent,"Final validation includes 22 reconciliation regressions and 8 compiled CLI/packaging/flag checks, typecheck, test typecheck, source docstring lint and public-copy validation. The real CLI accepts flags before the snapshot argument and emits compact TOON/JSON with git absent. Aggregate core compensation failures now return a typed recovery_required refusal with a remedy, preserving later writes. No separate lint script is configured; the maintained source/docstring gate and whitespace validation are used. Full npm/Bun release gates remain on CI."
  "2026-10-21T20:58:42.931Z",codex-agent,"All six linked commands passed: 22 reconciliation tests, 8 compiled CLI/packaging/flag checks, typecheck, test typecheck, docstring lint and the 93-item public-copy validation. Local strict health separately reports environment host skew from an already-installed extension and bootstrap fence drift; this does not establish a fresh-checkout CI verdict, which remains required. Existing tracker-reconciliation items and merge-driver files are untouched."
  "2026-10-21T21:02:51.457Z",codex-agent,"Initial full CI passed at 881d156: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-beads/actions/runs/39675043717 . Both npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed on Node 22 and 26, 377/377 tests per gate, zero failures/skips, 9 measured source files at 100% lines/branches/functions. A final real-clock regression then exposed ambiguous timestamp rollback; compensation now uses exact core history versions, and legacy checkpoints without a version mapping refuse before writing. Reverting only this compensation fix fails its shared-timestamp assertion. All six linked commands passed again with 24 reconciliation tests plus 8 CLI/packaging/flag checks. PR #160 holds final-head CI evidence and remains ready for review; full CI must rerun after this fix. Existing tracker-reconciliation items remain untouched. Package-level risk: legacy checkpoints need trustworthy version mapping before reversible application. SDK gap observed: timestamp-based restoration can select a later mutation sharing the same timestamp; no upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:18.007Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR #160: pulled the remote feature head and merged current origin/main (298d064). Read all comments on the single unresolved thread PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6u_usc and the latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff findings were present. Verified that missing live identities reach digest(undefined), and field-object insertion order incorrectly changes acknowledgement equality. Plan: compare supported fields directly, cover missing identities and reordered fields in real non-git trackers, verify compiled CLI refusal exit 2, run behavioral reverts and both unchanged full release gates. Whole-PR review checks the same undefined-hash and field-equality defect classes. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:22.727Z",codex-agent,"Confirmed the review finding with both new SDK regressions failing on the original implementation: missing identity threw ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE instead of the typed ack_mismatch; reversed matching field insertion order falsely returned ack_mismatch. Implemented field-by-field equality over RECONCILE_FIELDS with explicit missing-identity refusal. Tests also assert no base is saved and tracker items are preserved on refusal. Extended the real compiled CLI non-git test to require exit 2 and ack_mismatch before successfully acknowledging the same source. Self-review of the whole PR found no other potentially undefined digest input or serialized field-object equality; remaining digests bind source strings, arrays or explicit revision/plan objects. No outside-diff findings were reported."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:26.893Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6u_usc: reverted ONLY acknowledgeBeadsSnapshot to its pre-review function body and ran node --test --test-name-pattern='acknowledgement (refuses missing|accepts matching)' test/reconcile.test.ts. Both regressions failed (0/2 passed): missing identity produced ERR_INVALID_ARG_TYPE, reordered equal fields produced false ack_mismatch. Restored the fixed function; the identical command then passed 2/2. Full node --test test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts passed 27/27, zero failures/skips; pm test pm-beads-i59r --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 --author codex-agent also passed the registered command (27/27). Production build and test type compilation passed. npm ci and regenerated changelog/check passed. dist is generated and untracked in this repo. Full isolated npm release gate is now running; the Bun gate follows sequentially."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:31.777Z",codex-agent,"Existing infrastructure limitation is tracked separately in pm-beads-v9r1. Isolated pinned pm health --strict-exit --require-merge-drivers reports merge_fence_drift:2 with the committed .gitattributes (identical to origin/main); npm ci generates a -merge to merge=text policy change for the extensions subtree. That unrelated generated change was restored. No pending merge receipt or history drift was found in baseline health. Normal-home health also reports existing global extension-host skew, outside this package change. History remains append-only; no dependency bump, history repair or extension policy change is part of this review fix."
  "2026-10-22T12:26:34.633Z",codex-agent,"Full release gate passed with CI-style isolated home and Git configuration: env HOME=$(mktemp -d) GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1 npm run release:check. Node 24.19.0: 381/381 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped; 9 source files measured at unchanged 100% lines/branches/functions. Docstrings: 74/74 declarations across 9 files. Production audit: 0 vulnerabilities. Build, workflow contract, npm package dry-run, changelog check, publish provenance and version-derived changelog date contracts all passed. No timeout or retry was needed. The Bun release gate is running sequentially with the same isolation."
  "2026-10-22T12:29:38.555Z",codex-agent,"Final review-round validation: both CI-style isolated full release gates passed at unchanged thresholds: npm run release:check and bun run release:check each passed 381/381 tests, 0 failed, 0 skipped, with 9 source files at 100% lines/branches/functions and 74/74 documented declarations. Production audit, package dry-run, changelog and release contracts passed in each gate. Node 24.19.0, Bun 1.3.5. No timeout, retry or CI substitution was needed. Rebuilt generated dist; it is not committed by this repo. Behavioral reversion of only acknowledgeBeadsSnapshot failed both new regressions; restored implementation passed both and the full 27-test reconciliation/compiled CLI command. The linked pm runner passed 1/1 selected command (27 tests). Thread PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6u_usc is fixed; no outside-diff findings or evidence-backed refusals remain. All review threads stay untouched. Existing merge-fence health drift is the open follow-up pm-beads-v9r1; normal-home extension-host skew is also pre-existing. No other new pm CLI/SDK defect was established. Keep this feature in progress for orchestrator verification and release only the claim."
  "2026-10-22T14:45:38.271Z",codex-agent,"New review round after 57b2713: pulled the remote head; main is already included (298d064), so no merge was needed. Reused this item after context/search/open-item orientation. Read every unresolved review thread and the latest CodeRabbit review. PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vPCWz is valid: title-only import fills description from title, so the original file is not a matching acknowledgement. PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vPCW4 is valid: canonical tags and dependencies accept malformed JSON or non-string arrays. Plan: retain importer compatibility, document export-after-import before acknowledgement, execute both documented workflows in real non-git trackers, validate both collection fields at the shared record boundary, and prove refusal occurs before item/history/base writes. Self-review all public snapshot entrypoints for the same validation gap. No outside-diff findings were present. Existing merge-fence follow-up pm-beads-v9r1 stays out of scope."
  "2026-10-22T14:48:51.936Z",codex-agent,"Implemented both new findings. README and the worked example now bootstrap by importing, exporting the normalized live tracker, then acknowledging that export; the typed mismatch remedy and CLI help explain the same recovery. A regression executes the actual commands from both documents against title-only records with only pinned node/pm on PATH, without git. Shared canonical record validation now requires tags and dependencies to be JSON arrays containing only strings. Regressions cover invalid JSON, scalar/object/null values, non-string and nested array members in incoming/base/live classifier inputs, acknowledgement, planning, tampered reviewed-plan application and correctly checksummed persisted bases. Real SDK tests verify item snapshots, history bytes and the acknowledged base remain unchanged on refusal. Initial regressions failed 3/3 against the previous code/docs, then passed 3/3 after the fixes. Full-PR self-review found the same misleading import-first recovery in the typed remedy/help and corrected it; every public canonical snapshot entrypoint uses the shared validation boundary."
  "2026-10-22T14:50:57.043Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proof for PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vPCW4: reverted ONLY assertRecords to its pre-round function body, leaving all tests and other implementation changes intact. node --test --test-name-pattern=\"canonical SDK collection|invalid canonical collections\" test/reconcile.test.ts failed 2/2 tests: the pure classifier accepted malformed collections and application accepted a tampered malformed-tags plan (Missing expected rejection). Restored validation. For PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vPCWz, independently reverted ONLY README.md and ONLY examples/snapshot-reconciliation.md; node --test --test-name-pattern=\"documented import-export\" test/reconcile-cli.test.ts failed 1/1 in each experiment with ack_mismatch. The test executes both published code blocks against real title-only imports. All fixed files were restored after each experiment. With everything restored, node --test --test-name-pattern=\"canonical SDK collection|invalid canonical collections|documented import-export\" test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts passed 3/3, including the forged persisted-base and unchanged-history assertions."
  "2026-10-22T14:50:58.694Z",codex-agent,"No importer behavior or dependency pin changed. Shared validation covers acknowledgement, incoming/base/live classification, persisted base reads and reclassification before plan application. The malformed collection regression verifies both tags and dependencies, multiple malformed representations, unchanged live snapshots and byte-identical item histories after refusal. Documentation retains full-snapshot empty/default semantics and explains why the normalized live export must be acknowledged after import. Prior missing-identity/key-order regressions remain intact. Existing merge-fence follow-up pm-beads-v9r1 is unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T14:52:16.053Z",codex-agent,"The existing linked reconciliation/compiled CLI command passed 30/30 tests, zero failures/skips, through pm test pm-beads-i59r --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 --author codex-agent (1/1 selected registered command). Source build, test type compilation, 75/75 documented declarations across 9 files, npm ci, and changelog regeneration/check passed. The full npm release gate is now running with isolated home and Git configuration; Bun follows sequentially at unchanged thresholds. No local timeout or retry has occurred."
  "2026-10-22T14:55:03.919Z",codex-agent,"The full isolated npm run release:check passed at unchanged thresholds: 384/384 tests, zero failures/skips; 9 measured source files at 100% lines, branches and functions; 75/75 documented declarations. Build, type checking, workflow contracts, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), package dry-run, changelog and publish/date contracts all passed. Node 24.19.0. No timeout or retry was needed. The full isolated Bun gate is now running sequentially."
  "2026-10-22T14:57:22.302Z",codex-agent,"Final round validation for PR #160: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both passed with isolated home and Git configuration at unchanged thresholds. Each gate passed 384/384 tests, 0 failed, 0 skipped, with 9 source files at 100% lines/branches/functions and 75/75 documented declarations. Typecheck, build, workflow validation, zero-vulnerability production audit, package dry-run, changelog, publish provenance and date contracts passed. Node 24.19.0; Bun 1.3.5. No timeout, retry or CI substitution was needed. The linked reconciliation/compiled CLI command passed 30/30. Reverting only assertRecords failed both collection regressions; independently reverting each documentation file failed the executable workflow with ack_mismatch; restoring all fixes passed the three new regressions. Shared validation and all import-then-acknowledge guidance/help were self-reviewed. Both unresolved findings are fixed; no outside-diff findings or refusals remain. Prior fixes remain intact. Generated dist was rebuilt and is untracked by this repository. Existing follow-up pm-beads-v9r1 is unchanged; no new pm CLI/SDK bug or UX gap was established. Keep the item in progress for orchestrator verification, release the claim, and leave review threads untouched."
  "2026-10-22T16:21:41.558Z",codex-agent,"New review round after b19dbc2: worktree was clean, remote feature head was pulled, and main 298d064 is already included. Reused this item after context/search/open-item orientation. Fetched every unresolved thread with all comments and the latest CodeRabbit review; no outside-diff findings were present. PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vRcX7 is valid: Beads projects only blocked_by relationships, but reconciliation replaces or clears the entire SDK dependency collection. Plan to use the pinned SDK kind-scoped dependency removals/additions under the transaction, preserving unrelated edge records and provenance instead of reconstructing the whole collection. PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vRcYJ requires regression checks for flag-first positional selection and typed snapshot read failures. Review saved-plan input/output error handling for the same untyped I/O defect class. Prior fixes and existing follow-up pm-beads-v9r1 remain intact."
  "2026-10-22T16:32:12.929Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vRcX7 with kind-scoped SDK dependency deltas. Read the current item immediately before constructing link-step options, add only new blocked_by targets and remove only obsolete targets with explicit kind=blocked_by selectors. Other kinds and retained blocker records are never rebuilt, so timestamps, author and provenance are preserved. Regression reads authoritative stored metadata through public SDK locateItem/readLocatedItem, verifies related and verifies edges (including a related edge sharing a removed blocker target), and exercises adding, replacing and clearing all blockers. This is stronger than rebuilding a merged whole collection; the pinned SDK rejects empty replaceDeps and whole replacements reconstruct records. No clearDeps or replaceDeps remains in reconciliation."
  "2026-10-22T16:32:13.912Z",codex-agent,"Implemented PRRT_kwDOSZpl5M6vRcYJ by reusing the existing positional-input parser with additive source/plan value flags. Snapshot reads now refuse invalid_snapshot and plan-output writes refuse invalid_plan. Tests cover flags before the path, value flags and equals syntax, missing files, directory inputs, and unwritable plan destinations; compiled CLI tests exercise --acknowledge before the snapshot and require typed errors. Self-review found an additional dependency flag serialization instance: an unresolved literal ID containing source_kind=external was interpreted as SDK flag fields. JSON-quoting IDs preserves their data boundary; the real-tracker regression now rejects the unresolved literal without changing items, history or the acknowledged base."
  "2026-10-22T16:32:15.064Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral revert proofs: reverting ONLY mutationOptions to its pre-round function body made node --test --test-name-pattern=\"preserves local dependency|identifiers as data\" test/reconcile.test.ts fail 2/2 (unrelated edge loss; Missing expected rejection for identifier reinterpretation). Reverting ONLY runReconcile and rebuilding dist made node --test --test-name-pattern=\"reconcile CLI selects|compiled CLI acknowledges\" test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts fail 2/2. Restored source and rebuilt dist after the experiment. With fixes restored, the combined four targeted regressions passed 4/4. The earlier full reconciliation/CLI run passed 32/32 before adding the identifier regression. Build, test type compilation, docstrings and whitespace checks passed. Host UX observation: an untyped handler I/O failure can be obscured by the pinned host fallback as an unrelated unknown-option error; typed refusals avoid that path here. No upstream issue was filed."
  "2026-10-22T16:33:13.491Z",codex-agent,"The registered node --test test/reconcile.test.ts test/reconcile-cli.test.ts command passed 33/33 tests, zero failures/skips, through pm test pm-beads-i59r --run --only-last --progress --timeout 600 --author codex-agent (1/1 selected command). All prior acknowledgement, canonical collection, documentation and recovery regressions remain green. Build, test typecheck, 75/75 documented declarations, npm ci, changelog regeneration/check and whitespace validation passed. The full isolated npm release gate is running; Bun follows sequentially at unchanged thresholds. Existing committed history prefixes and public-safe tracked additions were independently checked."
  "2026-10-22T16:35:38.232Z",codex-agent,"Full isolated npm run release:check passed at unchanged thresholds: 387/387 tests, zero failures/skips; 9 measured source files at 100% lines/branches/functions; 75/75 documented declarations. Typecheck, build, workflow contract, production audit (zero vulnerabilities), package dry-run, changelog and release provenance/date contracts all passed. Node 24.19.0. No timeout or gate retry was needed. The full Bun gate is running sequentially with isolated home and Git configuration."
  "2026-10-22T16:38:28.673Z",codex-agent,"Final round validation: full npm run release:check and bun run release:check passed sequentially with isolated homes and Git configuration, at unchanged thresholds. Each gate passed 387/387 tests, zero failures/skips, 9 source files at 100% lines/branches/functions and 75/75 documented declarations. Typecheck, build, workflow checks, zero-vulnerability production audit, package dry-run, changelog and release provenance/date contracts passed. Node 24.19.0; Bun 1.3.5. No local timeout or full-gate retry occurred. The linked reconciliation/compiled CLI command passed 33/33. Function-only reverts failed 2/2 dependency regressions and 2/2 CLI regressions; compiled output was rebuilt for the CLI proof and all four targeted checks passed after restoring fixes. Both unresolved review findings are fixed; self-review additionally fixed dependency ID flag serialization and typed plan-output failures. Other dependency kinds and original provenance survive add/replace/clear; flags and values are excluded from snapshot path selection. Existing fixes and follow-up pm-beads-v9r1 are unchanged. The pinned host fallback can obscure untyped handler errors; covered adapter I/O failures now return typed refusals. No upstream issue was filed. Rebuilt dist remains untracked by repository policy. Keep this item in progress for orchestrator verification and release only the claim. No review replies, resolutions, merge or package release."
